### Package naming convention
- `com.bookreads.core.pref` — corePref module
- `com.bookreads.core.common` — coreCommon module
- `com.bookreads.di` — diApp module
- `com.bookreads.navigation` — navigation module

### DI pattern: `expect/actual` Koin modules
Every module with platform differences exposes an `expect val fooModule: Module` in `commonMain`, with `actual val` in each platform source set.

### `webMain` is a custom source set
The `webMain` source set is NOT a standard KMP name — it's a custom intermediate source set configured in the convention plugin (or elsewhere in the build) to aggregate `js` and `wasmJs` targets. Both `js { browser() }` and `wasmJs { browser() }` share `webMain` sources. Web uses `PrefServiceMemory` (no DataStore, no filesystem).

### `PrefPathProvider` interface placement
The `PrefPathProvider` interface is **not** in `commonMain` — it is duplicated in each of `androidMain`, `iosMain`, and `jvmMain`. The `webMain` module does not define it at all (no DataStore used there). The actual `PrefPathProvider` implementations are provided by `diApp`'s platform modules (`appPlatformModule`).
